description: Encode human corrections as Cursor rules instead of one-off apologies
alwaysApply: true
---

# Capture corrections as rules

When the human corrects a generation mistake, do not only fix the code.

1. Fix the instance.
2. Add a focused `.mdc` under `.cursor/rules/` named for the mistake.
3. Put a failing example and the required shape in the rule.
4. Product behavior gets an outcome Minitest. Agent process (how to write Rails) gets a Cursor `.mdc`. Do not add Minitest that reads source files to police style.

One concern per file. Keep it under 50 lines. These rules are meant to be copied into other greenfield Rails apps.
